+### Sites behind two-factor sign-in: attach to the user's Chrome
+
+Two-factor sign-in can fail in the bundled browser. Ask the user to install
+Playwright's Chrome extension (it shows as "Playwright Extension") in their
+everyday Chrome and sign in there, then attach to it:
+
+```bash
+node "$SKILL_DIR/scripts/pw.js" attach --extension=chrome
+```
+
+The command waits until the user approves the connection in Chrome and picks a
+tab, so run it in the background or with a long timeout. Pass the session name
+it prints to later commands (`-s=<session>`). You are now acting in the user's
+real tab with their account: navigation and clicks happen in front of them, so
+change nothing they have not asked for. Run commands from the artifact
+directory, because the CLI writes page snapshots to `.playwright-cli/` in the
+current directory and they can hold the signed-in account's data. Finish with
+`detach`.
+
